            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Entry-level engineers earn ₹6–9 LPA in India and $85K–$105K in the US. With 3–5 years of experience and cloud certification, salaries reach ₹15–25 LPA and $130K–$160K.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Is Data Engineering a good career in 2026?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;Yes. It remains among the highest-paid, fastest-growing tech disciplines. The rise of AI and LLM-powered systems has made pipeline infrastructure more critical than ever.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        },
        {
          &quot;name&quot;: &quot;What is the difference between ETL and ELT?&quot;,
          &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Question&quot;,
          &quot;acceptedAnswer&quot;: {
            &quot;text&quot;: &quot;ETL transforms data before loading it to the destination, common in legacy systems. ELT loads raw data first and transforms it inside the warehouse — the default for cloud-native stacks using dbt, BigQuery, and Snowflake.&quot;,
            &quot;@type&quot;: &quot;Answer&quot;
          }
        }
